{"id":"a3","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":3,"of":16,"title":"One and many","titleHe":"יָחִיד וְרַבִּים","goal":"Form plurals, and recognise the irregular ones you'll use daily.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Masculine nouns take ־ִים, feminine nouns take ־וֹת. The vowels inside the word usually shorten when the ending is added."},{"type":"table","caption":"Regular plurals","head":["singular","plural"],"rows":[["סֵפֶר — book","סְפָרִים"],["יֶלֶד — boy","יְלָדִים"],["מוֹרָה — teacher (f.)","מוֹרוֹת"],["מִשְׁפָּחָה — family","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"The ending does not always match the gender. שֻׁלְחָן is masculine but pluralises שֻׁלְחָנוֹת; שָׁנָה is feminine but goes שָׁנִים. The gender doesn't change — only the ending is irregular."},{"type":"table","caption":"The irregulars worth memorising","head":["singular","plural"],"rows":[["אִישׁ — man","אֲנָשִׁים"],["אִשָּׁה — woman","נָשִׁים"],["בַּיִת — house","בָּתִּים"],["בֵּן — son","בָּנִים"],["בַּת — daughter","בָּנוֹת"],["שָׁנָה — year","שָׁנִים"]]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אִישׁ","en":"man","translit":"ish"},{"he":"אִשָּׁה","en":"woman","translit":"isha"},{"he":"אֲנָשִׁים","en":"people, men","translit":"anashim"},{"he":"נָשִׁים","en":"women","translit":"nashim"},{"he":"בָּתִּים","en":"houses","translit":"batim"},{"he":"סְפָרִים","en":"books","translit":"sfarim"},{"he":"יְלָדִים","en":"children","translit":"yeladim"},{"he":"שָׁנָה","en":"year","translit":"shana"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["fails","man","the city","red"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אִישׁ","translit":"ish"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["woman","teacher (f.)","secret","stairs"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אִשָּׁה","translit":"isha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["grandson","firmament, sky","people, men","tooth"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אֲנָשִׁים","translit":"anashim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["guest","orange","Shvat (Jan–Feb)","women"],"correct":3,"prompt":"נָשִׁים","translit":"nashim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["road","houses","fact","shy"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בָּתִּים","translit":"batim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["books","prophet","shop","fridge"],"correct":0,"prompt":"סְפָרִים","translit":"sfarim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["goat","onion","joy","children"],"correct":3,"prompt":"יְלָדִים","translit":"yeladim"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “people, men”?","options":["מִצְטַעֵר","הוֹרִים","שַׁחַר","אֲנָשִׁים"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אִישׁ","man"],["אִשָּׁה","woman"],["אֲנָשִׁים","people, men"],["נָשִׁים","women"],["בָּתִּים","houses"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"Regular plurals — book?","options":["מוֹרוֹת","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת","סְפָרִים","יְלָדִים"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “women”?","options":["נָשִׁים","יוֹצֵא","תַּרְנְגֹלֶת","קְרִיאָה"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Regular plurals — family?","options":["יְלָדִים","סְפָרִים","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת","מוֹרוֹת"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"The irregulars worth memorising — daughter?","options":["בָּתִּים","בָּנוֹת","נָשִׁים","אֲנָשִׁים"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Regular plurals — boy?","options":["מוֹרוֹת","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת","סְפָרִים","יְלָדִים"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"The irregulars worth memorising — house?","options":["אֲנָשִׁים","בָּנִים","נָשִׁים","בָּתִּים"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “people, men” in Hebrew","answer":"אֲנָשִׁים","hint":"anashim"}]}